      "Takumi laughed.",
      "\"You too, Mr. Connors. You must respect your food,\" Mrs. Kurogane said.",
      "\"Sorry, Sensei,\" said Takumi. He picked up another egg and cracked it into his bowl. Daichi cracked the other two.",
      "\"I'll whisk,\" said Daichi.",
      "\"Pick the shells out first,\" said Takumi.",
      "Daichi took the bowl and mixed the eggs.",
      "\"Good,\" said Mrs. Kurogane. \"While your partner is doing that, the other person can start dicing the onions for the omelet rice.\"",
      "Takumi picked up an onion and a knife. He placed the onion on the cutting board and cut off the top and bottom. He sliced it in half and started cutting big slices. \"This is easy,\" he said.",
      "\"Mr. Connors,\" said Mrs. Kurogane. \"You have to peel the brown skin from the onion before you start slicing.\"",
      "The university student at the next table smiled and looked away.",
      "\"Oops. Sorry,\" said Takumi.",
      "Mrs. Kurogane shook her head. \"Now, add a pinch of salt and a bit of milk to the eggs,\" she said.",
      "\"How much milk?\" asked Daichi.",
      "\"Just a little bit,\" Mrs. Kurogane said.",
      "Daichi held up a full cup. \"Is this enough?\" he asked.",
      "\"Two teaspoons, Mr. Tachibana,\" Mrs. Kurogane said, shaking her head.",
      "\"Oh, okay,\" Daichi said.",
      "\"She should have said that,\" whispered Takumi.",
      "Daichi nodded and measured two teaspoons of milk into the eggs.",
      "\"You may want more salt,\" said Takumi.",
      "\"I think you're right,\" said Daichi.",
