  "culturalNotes": [
      {
          "title": "What is Manzai?",
          "text": "Manzai (漫才) is a traditional style of Japanese stand-up comedy. It usually has two performers: the boke (ボケ) and the tsukkomi (ツッコミ). The boke is the funny one. They say silly things, make mistakes, or misunderstand situations. The tsukkomi is the serious one. They react to the boke's mistakes, often with a light slap or a sharp comment. Manzai is very popular in Japan, especially in the Osaka and Kansai region. Famous manzai pairs appear regularly on Japanese television. The word manzai comes from an old Japanese performance tradition dating back over 1,000 years. In the story, Karin (Miss Oi) thinks Daichi and Takumi are a manzai team because Daichi often does something silly or reckless (the boke), while Takumi reacts with surprise or concern (the tsukkomi). Their cooking mistakes and arguments reminded her of a comedy performance!"
      }
    ],
